  "status": "ok",
  "summary_en": "Converts the layers of an Ocean Spectrum COP into an animated ocean surface. It evaluates them at a given time to produce the surface height and horizontal displacement.",
  "inputs": [
    "amplitude: the amplitude layer from an Ocean Spectrum COP",
    "frequency: the frequency layer from an Ocean Spectrum COP",
    "phase: the phase layer from an Ocean Spectrum COP"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Scale: overall multiplier on wave amplitude; higher values produce taller waves",
    "Chop: sharpens wave crests and flattens troughs by pushing the surface toward the peaks",
    "Time: the time at which the ocean surface is evaluated",
    "Ocean Size: world-space size of the input spectrum; should match the Ocean Size of the Ocean Spectrum COP",
    "Outputs: height (vertical surface height), cusp (wave peak sharpness), dir (horizontal displacement, which can distort textures such as foam through the Distort COP)"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "The page has no separate warning section. If Ocean Size does not match the Ocean Spectrum COP, the horizontal displacement is scaled incorrectly."
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Transforme les couches d'un spectre d'océan en surface animée, en donnant la hauteur et le déplacement horizontal à un instant donné, avec une taille d'océan qui doit correspondre au spectre."
}
